From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:16:55 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] nl80211: keep the netdev of a BSS that becomes the first BSS

Depends on 601-ucode_support.patch.

The ucode BSS deletion and set_bss_order make another BSS the first BSS
of an interface with set_first_bss(). The netdev of that BSS can be one
that hostapd created (added_if). Where the driver is shared with another
interface, a DISABLE of the interface then removed that netdev
(hostapd_cleanup_driver() -> hostapd_if_remove()), and the next ENABLE
failed: hostapd_driver_init() finds the shared driver through the
netdev of the first BSS, so the driver init ended with "Could not read
interface ... flags: No such device".

Clear added_if of the new first BSS, so that its netdev stays at a
deinit, as the netdev of a first BSS that hostapd did not create does.
The old first BSS keeps its flag: hostapd still removes only the netdevs
it created for a BSS that is not first, and an MLD netdev of another
owner stays. Also move drv->ifindex to the new first BSS, as the
removal of a first BSS does.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>

--- a/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c
+++ b/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c
@@ -12223,10 +12223,15 @@ static int driver_nl80211_set_first_bss(
 		if (tbss->next != bss)
 			continue;
 
+		/* The netdev of the first BSS stays at a deinit, and the next
+		 * driver init finds the driver through it */
+		bss->added_if = 0;
+
 		tbss->next = bss->next;
 		bss->next = drv->first_bss;
 		drv->first_bss = bss;
 		drv->ctx = bss->ctx;
+		drv->ifindex = bss->ifindex;
 		return 0;
 	}
 
